  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a reader paging through a list, I want the « page x / y » pill to be as easy to hit as the ‹ › buttons next to it, and to look like one control of the bar, so that the pager is one consistent Liquid Glass group.\n\n### Rule\n\n- \"As a general rule, a button needs a hit region of at least 44x44 pt\" — [HIG › Buttons](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/buttons) (Best practices; page updated 2025-12-16).\n- \"Prefer using standard components in a toolbar. By default, standard buttons, text fields, headers, and footers have corner radii that are concentric with bar corners.\" — [HIG › Toolbars](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/toolbars) (updated 2025-12-16).\n- \"If you apply Liquid Glass effects to a custom control, do so sparingly.\" — [HIG › Materials](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/materials) (Liquid Glass; updated 2025-09-09).\n\n### What the app does (dev-swift @ `7a61018f`)\n\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Navigation/PagerPageMenu.swift:96-97`: the pill is `.padding(.horizontal, 12).padding(.vertical, 6).glassEffect(.regular, in: .capsule)`, the label of a `Menu` with `.buttonStyle(.plain)` (`:79`): body text plus 12 pt of padding, with no `minHeight` or `contentShape`. The title pill does it right (`ScreenTitle.swift:164-166`: `.frame(minHeight: 44)`, `.contentShape(.capsule)`).\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Navigation/PagerToolbar.swift:50-53`: on the iPad sidebar root the same pill goes into `ToolbarItemGroup(placement: .bottomBar)`, so its capsule sits on the bar group's own glass (the title pill hides the shared background, `ScreenTitle.swift:82`; this one does not).\n\n### Legacy at `87fe0d1c`\n\n`HFRswift/Swift/MainWindow.swift:1031-1068`: one custom glass surface (`hfrGlassSurface`) holding plain buttons; the page button is footnote text with `.frame(minWidth: 74)` under `.controlSize(.small)`. Also small, no nested glass.\n\n### Class\n\n**(a) defect** (touch target: accessibility, whatever legacy does). The nested capsule is to confirm on a rendering.\n\n### Proposed fix and check\n\n- `.frame(minHeight: 44)` and `.contentShape(.capsule)` on the pill; in the `.bottomBar` placement, a plain `Menu` label that lets the toolbar supply the glass.\n- Mac check: Accessibility Inspector hit-area audit of the pill (tab root strip and iPad bottom bar, default and AX sizes); iPad regular width, Messages with several pages: no capsule inside a capsule, in light, dark and Reduce Transparency.\n\nRelated: #980 (same pill), #545, #1138.\n\nFound by #866 (cloud/r866-fable, Fable 5.2)",
